---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="PROFILE｜Nishikino"
  description=""
>

<section id="profileSection" class="relative min-h-screen overflow-hidden">

  <!-- Background -->
  <img
    id="profileBg1"
    src="/images/profile-bg.png"
    alt="Profile background"
    class="profile-bg profile-bg-front absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover select-none pointer-events-none"
    draggable="false"
  />

  <img
    id="profileBg2"
    src="/images/profile-bg-message.png"
    alt=""
    class="profile-bg profile-bg-back absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover select-none pointer-events-none"
    draggable="false"
  />

  <!-- Overlay -->
  <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/27"></div>

  <!-- Content -->
  <div
    class="relative z-10 mx-auto flex min-h-screen max-w-[1700px]
           flex-col items-center justify-between
           px-5 py-24
           sm:px-8 sm:py-28
           lg:flex-row lg:px-20 lg:py-24"
  >

    <!-- Left -->
    <div
      id="profileLeft"
      class="profile-content w-full
             lg:w-[30%]"
    >

      <p
        class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.35em] text-white
               sm:text-sm sm:tracking-[0.55em]"
        style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;"
      >
        PROFILE
      </p>

      <h1
        class="mt-4 text-4xl font-light text-white
               sm:text-6xl
               lg:mt-6 lg:text-7xl"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        NISHIKINO
      </h1>

      <p
        class="mt-6 text-xs leading-6 text-white/90
               sm:text-base sm:leading-10
               lg:mt-8"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        
        <br />
        A video creator who loves Japanese traditions and architecture,
        <br />
        exploring new ways to express my ideas through my work.
        <br /><br />

        I enjoy visiting famous places,
        <br />
        capturing landscapes and moments on camera,
        <br />
        and turning the things I love into creations of my own.
      </p>

    </div>


    <!-- Center -->
    <div class="hidden lg:block lg:w-[18%]"></div>


    <!-- Right -->
    <div
      class="profile-content delay mt-10 w-full space-y-5
             sm:mt-12 sm:space-y-6
             lg:mt-0 lg:w-[34%] lg:space-y-6"
    >

      <!-- INTRODUCTION -->
      <div
        id="introductionCard"
        class="profile-card rounded-[24px] border border-white/20
               bg-transparent p-5
               sm:rounded-[34px] sm:p-8"
      >

        <p
          class="text-[9px] tracking-[0.35em] text-white/60
                 sm:text-xs sm:tracking-[0.45em]"
        >
          INTRODUCTION
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white
                 sm:mt-5 sm:space-y-4 sm:text-base sm:leading-8"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >

          <p>
            The name <strong>錦乃</strong> brings together two ideas:
            <strong>錦</strong>, a word associated with rich, colorful beauty,
            like the patterns of brocade, and <strong>乃</strong>,
            which gives the name an elegant, classical character.
            <br />
            I combined the two to create a name that conveys
            something rich, beautiful, and timeless.
          </p>

          <div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-4 text-white/90">
            <p>Yuya Tousaka</p>
            <p>Age: 23</p>
            <p>Birthday: May 4, 2003</p>
            <p>Hometown: Ota, Gunma, Japan</p>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>


      <!-- MESSAGE -->
      <div
        id="messageCard"
        class="profile-card rounded-[24px] border border-white/20
               bg-transparent p-5
               sm:rounded-[34px] sm:p-8"
      >

        <p
          class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.4em] text-white/60
                 sm:text-xs sm:tracking-[0.45em]"
        >
          MESSAGE
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-5 text-[13px] leading-7 text-white
                 sm:text-base sm:leading-8"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >

          <p>
            Welcome. It is a pleasure to have you here.<br>
          </p>

          <p class="mt-4">
            I first came to be known for my work recreating traditional
            Japanese landmarks in the globally popular sandbox game,
            <em>Minecraft</em>, sharing those creations under the name
            “Nishikino.”
          </p>

<details id="messageDetails" class="mt-6 group">

  <!-- Read More -->
  <summary
    id="messageSummary"
    class="cursor-pointer select-none text-rose-200 transition hover:text-white"
  >
    ▶ Read More
  </summary>


  <!-- MESSAGE DETAIL -->
  <div
    class="mt-6 space-y-6 text-[13px] leading-7 text-white/90
           sm:text-base sm:leading-8"
  >

    <p>
      I have loved cities and the energy of busy streets since I was young.
      My interest in Japanese traditions and architecture grew naturally from
      that fascination with places and the atmosphere they create.
      (To be honest, I was not originally someone who was especially interested
      in traditional Japanese architecture!)
    </p>

    <p>
      Everything began when I was in middle school and fell in love at first
      sight with the keep of Edo Castle depicted in the famous
      <em>Edo-zu Byōbu</em>, a historical folding screen depicting the city of Edo.
    </p>

    <p>
      In Minecraft, I originally wanted to build a sturdy house that enemies
      could not destroy in Survival Mode. That idea led me to build a castle
      keep, which became the starting point of my journey into architecture.
    </p>

    <p>
      From there, I began recreating real places simply because I wanted to be
      able to look at the places I loved whenever I wanted.
      Eventually, I realized that I could also recreate buildings and
      landscapes that no longer exist.
    </p>

    <p>
      Today, I explore cities and visit famous landmarks, castles,
      historic sites, and places connected to the Tokugawa family.
      I share the things I love in my own way through photography,
      video, and digital creations.
    </p>

    <p>
      I originally did all of this simply as a hobby, but as more people began
      to appreciate my work, I eventually started receiving commissions as well...!
    </p>

    <p>
      There is a Japanese saying, <em>suki koso mono no jōzu nare</em>,
      which is often translated as
      “Love what you do, and you will become good at it.”
      I have come to understand just how true those words are through my own
      experience.
    </p>

    <p>
      When it comes to architecture, my approach is fundamentally about
      reconstruction.
      I love creating buildings that go beyond the game itself and look
      almost indistinguishable from the real thing.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside of traditional Japanese architecture, I also enjoy watching
      gaming creators play a wide variety of Steam games,
      taking photographs and making videos,
      watching anime,
      and traveling and sightseeing without limiting myself to any particular
      style or destination.
      I am also interested in learning how to make great coffee,
      as well as fashion and beauty.
    </p>

    <p>
      Aside from Minecraft, my favorite games include
      <em>UNDERTALE</em> and <em>Deltarune</em>.
      I also tend to get really into YouTubers and voice actors.
      (There are a few in particular that I follow closely:
      a green YouTuber with a clover on his avatar who creates educational
      content,
      a YouTuber who lives at a school and periodically causes explosions
      — literally,
      and a male voice actor who has played several characters connected to
      other worlds.
      I also once considered attending a voice-acting school and was accepted
      through its audition process.)
    </p>

    <p>
      Once something catches my interest, I research it thoroughly,
      experience it for myself,
      and find my own way to preserve what I discover.
      Driven by pure curiosity and the strong energy that comes with it,
      I enjoy the entire process itself.
    </p>

  </div>

  <div class="message-actions">

    <a
      href="/en/profile/gallery"
      class="cursor-pointer select-none text-rose-200 transition hover:text-white"
    >
    ▶ Gallery
    </a>

    <button
      id="collapseMessage"
      type="button"
      class="cursor-pointer select-none text-rose-200 transition hover:text-white"
    >
    </button>

  </div>

</details>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<style>

.profile-bg{
  animation:profileFloat 12s ease-in-out infinite;
  transition:opacity .7s ease;
}

.profile-bg-front{
  opacity:1;
}

.profile-bg-back{
  opacity:0;
}

@keyframes profileFloat{
  0%{
    transform:scale(1.05) translateY(0px);
  }
  50%{
    transform:scale(1.08) translateY(-15px);
  }
  100%{
    transform:scale(1.05) translateY(0px);
  }
}

.profile-content{
  opacity:0;
  transform:translateY(80px) scale(.96);
  animation:profileAppear 1.2s cubic-bezier(.18,.89,.32,1.28) forwards;
}

.profile-content.delay{
  animation-delay:.25s;
}

@keyframes profileAppear{
  0%{
    opacity:0;
    transform:translateY(80px) scale(.96);
  }
  70%{
    opacity:1;
    transform:translateY(-12px) scale(1.02);
  }
  100%{
    opacity:1;
    transform:translateY(0) scale(1);
  }
}

.profile-card{
  transition:transform .6s ease, background .6s ease;
  animation:cardFloat 8s ease-in-out infinite;
}

.profile-card:nth-child(2){
  animation-delay:1s;
}

@keyframes cardFloat{
  0%{
    transform:translateY(0);
  }
  50%{
    transform:translateY(-8px);
  }
  100%{
    transform:translateY(0);
  }
}

details summary{
  list-style:none;
}

details summary::-webkit-details-marker{
  display:none;
}



:global(html) {
  color-scheme: light;
}

:global(body) {
  color-scheme: light;
  -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
}


.profile-content p,
.profile-content h1,
.profile-content h2,
.profile-content h3,
.profile-content strong {
  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


/* PROFILE label */

.profile-content > p:first-child {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


/* PROFILE name */

.profile-content h1 {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


/* Profile introduction text */

.profile-content > p:not(:first-child) {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}


.profile-card {
  forced-color-adjust: none;

  background-color: transparent !important;

  border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2) !important;
}


.profile-card > p:first-child {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card > div {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


.profile-card > div p {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card > div > div.border-t {
  border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15) !important;

  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}


.profile-card > div > div.border-t p {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}

#messageDetails {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


#messageDetails > div {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


#messageDetails > div p {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}

#messageSummary {
  color: rgb(254, 205, 211) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgb(254, 205, 211);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


#messageSummary:hover {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


#messageDetails a {
  color: rgb(254, 205, 211) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgb(254, 205, 211);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


#messageDetails a:hover {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


@media (max-width: 639px) {

  .profile-content,
  .profile-content *,
  .profile-card,
  .profile-card *,
  #messageDetails,
  #messageDetails *,
  #messageSummary {
    forced-color-adjust: none;
  }

  .profile-card {
    background-color: transparent !important;
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2) !important;
  }

  .profile-content > p:first-child,
  .profile-content h1 {
    color: #ffffff !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
  }

  .profile-content > p:not(:first-child) {
    font-size: 14px !important;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  }

  .profile-card > p:first-child {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .profile-card > div,
  .profile-card > div p {
    font-size: 14px !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
  }

  .profile-card > div > div.border-t,
  .profile-card > div > div.border-t p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);

    border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15) !important;
  }

  #messageDetails > div,
  #messageDetails > div p {
    font-size: 14px !important;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  }

  #messageSummary,
  #messageDetails a {
    color: rgb(254, 205, 211) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgb(254, 205, 211);
  }


  #profileSection.message-open #profileLeft,
  #profileSection.message-open #introductionCard {
    display: none !important;
  }

  #profileSection.message-open > div.relative.z-10 {
    justify-content: flex-start !important;
  }

  #profileSection.message-open #messageCard {
    width: 100% !important;
  }

}


@media (max-width: 639px) {

  #profileBg2 {
    object-position: center center !important;
  }

}

</style>

<script is:inline>
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {

  const section = document.getElementById("profileSection");
  const profileLeft = document.getElementById("profileLeft");
  const introductionCard = document.getElementById("introductionCard");
  const messageCard = document.getElementById("messageCard");

  const details = document.getElementById("messageDetails");
  const summary = document.getElementById("messageSummary");

  const bg1 = document.getElementById("profileBg1");
  const bg2 = document.getElementById("profileBg2");

  if (
    !section ||
    !profileLeft ||
    !introductionCard ||
    !messageCard ||
    !details ||
    !summary ||
    !bg1 ||
    !bg2
  ) return;


  details.addEventListener("toggle", () => {

    const isMobile = window.innerWidth <= 639;

    if (details.open) {

      /* Switch background */
      bg1.style.opacity = "0";
      bg2.style.opacity = "1";

      /* Show collapse button */
      summary.textContent = "  ▶ Collapse";


      if (isMobile) {

        profileLeft.style.display = "none";
        introductionCard.style.display = "none";

        /* Make MESSAGE full width */
        messageCard.style.width = "100%";

        /* Position MESSAGE toward the top */
        const content = section.querySelector(
          ".relative.z-10"
        );

        if (content) {
          content.style.justifyContent = "flex-start";
        }

      }

    } else {

      /* Restore background */
      bg1.style.opacity = "1";
      bg2.style.opacity = "0";

      /* Show read more button */
      summary.textContent = "Read More";


      if (isMobile) {

        profileLeft.style.display = "";
        introductionCard.style.display = "";
        messageCard.style.width = "";

        const content = section.querySelector(
          ".relative.z-10"
        );

        if (content) {
          content.style.justifyContent = "";
        }

      }

    }

  });

});
</script>


</Layout>
